{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a dual nickel/photoredox-catalyzed method for the direct carbamoylation of (hetero)aryl bromides at ambient temperature. The reaction utilizes 4-carbamoyl-1,4-dihydropyridines as precursors for carbamoyl radicals, which are intercepted by a nickel catalyst to form secondary and tertiary amides. The method is notable for its mild conditions, tolerance of sensitive functional groups, and ability to prepare amides with electron-poor or sterically hindered amine moieties without dehydrating agents.",
